arbeitnow:data-engineer-berlin-345637:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join the team rewriting the rules in private markets.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Moonfare delivers what few others can: the highly sought-after funds and hidden-gem investments that go beyond what most private banks offer. Every opportunity is subjected to a ruthless vetting process; the bar is unforgivingly high. The result? Institutional-quality portfolios for investors who demand more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team combines finance veterans with talent from tech, consulting, law and industries you’d never expect. Headquartered in Berlin, we operate from eight offices across Europe, the US and Asia.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you're ready to build what's next in private markets, let's talk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Engineer (m/f/d)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We're looking for a Data Engineer who has hands-on experience integrating&amp;nbsp;databases and external APIs, understands AWS infrastructure, and is comfortable working with tools like DBT to model and transform data. You'll&amp;nbsp;help build and scale our data platform from ingestion through to the&amp;nbsp;warehouse layer, powering AI Agents, BI, and business decisions across the&amp;nbsp;organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain data pipelines from ingestion through to storage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take end-to-end ownership of pipeline components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Model data using data lake and warehouse concepts, and contribute to performance improvements (partitioning, file formats, tuning)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply data governance and security practices in your work (least-privilege IAM, encryption, PII handling)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the team with data quality, coding consistency and data availability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with analysts and stakeholders to translate requirements into working data solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, formulate, and propose improvements to your own and your team’s practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Next Moonfarian:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2–4 years of hands-on experience building and maintaining data pipelines in production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Python and advanced SQL skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic Scala experience, or a willingness to pick it up
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If not, excellent domain of Java or C#&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with DBT (models, tests, documentation)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid working knowledge of AWS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with relational databases and data warehouses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident in Git, CI/CD, and modern deployment practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience with Docker&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solution-oriented, strong attention to detail, and open to feedback and mentorship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Apache Spark or a similar distributed processing framework&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of K8&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bash scripting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flyway or similar SQL migration tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If you feel you do not meet all of the requirements, we still encourage you to apply!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Values:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our clients come first, Moonfare comes second, and we prioritise ourselves third - Client-Centric Focus. &lt;/strong&gt;Putting clients first means creating value for them is essential. Placing Moonfare second signifies that our individual professional future at Moonfare depends on the company's commercial success. Prioritising ourselves third reflects our humility in putting clients and Moonfare before personal interests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We pursue excellence and honor our promises - Commitment to Excellence. &lt;/strong&gt;We hold ourselves to the highest standards, taking responsibility for our failures, and celebrating our successes. We commit to deadlines and stick to them and we learn from our mistakes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We are here to win and to celebrate our collective achievements - Win together.&lt;/strong&gt; We are mission-focused and think and act like owners. We exemplify the attitude we expect and each of us commits to do what it takes to succeed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We foster personal growth but each of us earns our place as a Moonfarian through merit - Growth and Merit. &lt;/strong&gt;We hire, retain, and develop exceptional people and invest in empowering them to excel. We must all earn our place at the table every day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We understand the important role that diversity plays in our success. Different backgrounds, experiences and ideas push us further and raise the bar. We’re committed to developing an inclusive and safe culture where everyone&amp;nbsp; — regardless of colour, race, religion, sex, origin, sexuality, disability, marital status, citizenship or gender identity — knows that they are an integral part of the team and can bring their full potential to their work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*Minimum investments vary according to jurisdiction.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</p>

arbeitnow:senior-localization-engineer-a:
&lt;div class="content-intro"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who is Tenable?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tenable® is the Exposure Management company. Over 40,000 organizations around the globe rely on Tenable to understand and reduce cyber risk. Our global employees support 65 percent of the Fortune 500, 50 percent of the Global 2000, and large government agencies. Come be part of our journey!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What makes Tenable such a great place to work?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ask a member of our team and they’ll answer, “Our people!” We work together to build and innovate best-in-class cybersecurity solutions for our customers; all while creating a culture of belonging, respect, and excellence where we can be our best selves. When you’re part of our #OneTenable team, you can expect to partner with some of the most talented and passionate people in the industry, and have the support and resources you need to do work that truly matters. We deliver results that exceed expectations and we win together!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Localization Engineer, Applied AI is a pivotal technical lead role responsible for the next-generation evolution of Tenable's established multilingual delivery infrastructure. This role requires a dual focus: providing strategic architectural direction while maintaining hands-on expertise in multilingual content engineering, system integration, and workflow automation. This is a unique opportunity to evolve our global content delivery platform — scalable and optimized for integrating AI-led technologies — accelerating the global delivery of multilingual content&lt;br&gt;across Tenable's international markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Sr Director of Globalisation, you will serve as the primary technical authority for the team, while evolving a system architecture that achieves tangible productivity outcomes through AI-led automation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead the shift from automated to AI-led localization: &lt;/strong&gt;Lead the evolution of AI/LLM-led workflows built for accelerated, simultaneous multi-language releases, focusing on product UI first.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Gradually extend the AI-led pipeline model across the content stack:&lt;/strong&gt; Take the principles proven in the product UI pipeline and, working with partner engineers, apply to other content areas — online documentation, marketing, and beyond, scale a consistent, AI-led delivery approach across Tenable's international content ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape standards and governance: &lt;/strong&gt;Define high-standard technical best practices, system hygiene norms, and engineering documentation that the wider team can build on as you are leading through the shift.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build intelligence into operations: &lt;/strong&gt;Complement existing reporting with AI-powered reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead, build and orchestrate: &lt;/strong&gt;Own hands-on delivery of key initiatives while directing contracted and distributed engineering partners on others — with the judgment to know which work to keep close and which to delegate effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You'll Need:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We're building at the frontier of AI-led localization — which means the landscape shifts fast, and so do we. We value curiosity and a genuine drive to learn at least as much as specific tool experience. Strong foundations plus the energy to grow are highly valued. Here is what we are looking for:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-forward mindset: &lt;/strong&gt;You're energized by the pace of change in AI tooling, follow new&amp;nbsp;developments actively, and bring that curiosity into your engineering work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LLM integration:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience integrating LLMs (ideally Claude/Anthropic) and&amp;nbsp;agentic steps into engineering workflows — building reliable, production-grade AI&amp;nbsp;pipelines and programmatic model improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pipeline architecture:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to design event-driven, API-first translation infrastructure — where content from repos, CMS platforms, and databases flows automatically into translation engines, triggered by code commits, content changes, or release events. This also includes web and content delivery workflows such as CMS-driven and proxy-based localization solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Internationalization &amp;amp; Localization engineering: &lt;/strong&gt;Strong i18n/l10n engineering&lt;br&gt;awareness — string externalisation, relevant frameworks, and deep familiarity with localization file formats and encoding conventions across content types.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Translation Management Systems: &lt;/strong&gt;Solid understanding of TMS principles -Translation Memory, Machine Translation, and next-generation integration frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding of &lt;strong&gt;CI/CD and DevOps&lt;/strong&gt; frameworks and principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong scripting ability &lt;/strong&gt;(Javascript, Python, Regex).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design for scale:&lt;/strong&gt; Solutions that generalise across content types and delivery channels where appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder communication: &lt;/strong&gt;Comfortable bridging engineering and non-engineering colleagues — linguists, project managers, developers, architects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documentation discipline: &lt;/strong&gt;Strong documentation habits — knowledge transfer is built into the role from day one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Distributed team collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Able to work effectively with distributed teams across multiple geographies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-AV1&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
